      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A foreach loop runs its body once for each value in an array. foreach (Light light in lights) hands the body one light at a time, in the variable light. There is no index to count: the loop ends after the last value. SwitchOff and SwitchOn turn every light of the array off, or on.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Lamps 3 holds four lights. You click 3 \xB7 All off. How many times does the line inside the loop run?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Press Play, select Lamps 3 and open Code Watch.\n2. Click 3 \xB7 All off, then 3 \xB7 All on.\n3. Remove one light from Lights, and click again."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
